---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PasswordRules from '@/components/PasswordRules.astro';
import { SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, SUPABASE_URL } from '@/lib/supabase-public';
import { url } from '@/lib/site';
import closed2027 from '@/data/sportmgr/1244761.json';

const captainsHref = url('/captains/');
const juniorEntriesHref = url('/juniors/closed/entries/');
const articlesHref = url('/captains/admin/articles/');
const shareHref = url('/captains/admin/share/');
const scoresHref = url('/captains/admin/minigame/');
---

<Base
  title="Administration"
  description="League Master lists, SquashLevels, website groups, the database, and the club, team and player details."
  noindex
>
  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container setup" id="setup-app" data-url={SUPABASE_URL} data-key={SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}>
      <h1>Administration</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        <strong>League Master</strong> lists club captains, team captains, and players. Those lists are read only. An email, name, or ES number saved on this website stays. A difference with League Master is listed under Differences. Phone stays on this website.
        <strong>Juniors</strong> lists the Junior County Closed entries submitted on this website. <strong>Beds Closed</strong> lists the County Closed entry list. Each person is tagged with the year, and email and mobile come from Sport Manager.
        <strong>SquashLevels</strong> shows each player’s level.
        <strong>Permissions</strong> is Users, Groups, and Roles, and only an admin sees it. Users is every League Master player. Update the email, ES number, and phone there, and change the password, turn the account off, or delete it when a login exists. A group gives one role. League Master fills the club, team, and player groups. Someone in those groups who is on SquashLevels also receives SL Player.
        <strong>Links</strong> joins a League Master player to their SquashLevels name when the names differ.
        <strong>Config</strong> shows each database table, how many rows it holds, how much space it uses, and a weekly graph of new rows. It also lists each outside service, the account name, where the password is kept, and how many rows that service has stored. Only an admin sees it.
        A club captain sees their club. A team captain sees their team. A player sees their own row. Nothing is emailed.
      </p>
      <p class="status" data-status role="status"></p>

      <div data-panel="signed-in" hidden>
        <p class="who" data-who></p>
        <p class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href={`${captainsHref}matches/`}>Matches</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" data-junior-link hidden href={juniorEntriesHref}>Junior entries</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href={articlesHref}>Articles</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" data-share-link hidden href={shareHref}>Shared content</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" data-scores-link hidden href={scoresHref}>Minigame mk4 results</a>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-lm-only data-tab-button="traffic" hidden>Traffic</button>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" href={`${captainsHref}profile/`}>Profile</a>
          <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-sign-out>Sign out</button>
        </p>
        <div data-workspace hidden>
          <nav class="admin-tabs" aria-label="Administration">
            <span class="tab-group">
              <span class="tab-label">League Master</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="site-club">Club</button>
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="site-team">Team</button>
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="site-player">Player</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group" data-juniors-nav hidden>
              <span class="tab-label">Juniors</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="juniors">Juniors</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group" data-beds-nav hidden>
              <span class="tab-label">Beds Closed</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="beds-closed">Players</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group" data-lm-only>
              <span class="tab-label">Marking</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="scores">Matches</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group">
              <span class="tab-label">SquashLevels</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="site-sl">SL</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group" data-lm-only>
              <span class="tab-label">Permissions</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-lm-only data-tab-button="members">Users</button>
                <button type="button" data-lm-only data-tab-button="permissions-groups">Groups</button>
                <button type="button" data-lm-only data-tab-button="permissions-roles">Roles</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group" data-lm-only>
              <span class="tab-label">Links</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="links">Links</button>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="tab-group" data-lm-only>
              <span class="tab-label">Config</span>
              <span class="tab-buttons">
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="database">Database</button>
                <button type="button" data-tab-button="integrations">Integrations</button>
              </span>
            </span>
          </nav>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="site-club">
            <h2>Club</h2>
            <p class="muted small" data-site-club-note></p>
            <div data-site-club></div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="site-team" hidden>
            <h2>Team</h2>
            <p class="muted small" data-site-team-note></p>
            <div data-site-team></div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="site-player" hidden>
            <h2>Player</h2>
            <p class="muted small" data-site-player-note></p>
            <div data-site-player-list></div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="juniors" hidden>
            <h2>Juniors</h2>
            <p class="muted small">Junior County Closed entries submitted on this website. An admin can correct every field, and add an entry after the public form has closed. Saving sends a short note to the Junior organisers. It does not send an email. An admin or a junior organiser places each entrant in the draw, in the order the names come out of the hat, then publishes that draw on the Juniors page.</p>
            <p class="actions"><button class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" type="button" data-add-junior hidden>Add an entry</button><span data-junior-draw-publish></span></p>
            <div data-new-junior hidden></div>
            <div class="overview-box juniors-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Player</th>
                    <th>Age group</th>
                    <th>Section</th>
                    <th>Club</th>
                    <th>Parent</th>
                    <th>Notes</th>
                    <th>Public name</th>
                    <th></th>
                    <th></th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-juniors-people></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="junior-draw" data-junior-draw hidden>
              <h3>The draw</h3>
              <p class="muted small">Press a name as it comes out of the hat. A draw can be one category, or several categories played together. Knockout fills the top half, then the bottom half. Round robin keeps one list, and each player plays every other player. Add the court and the time at Towers. Publish the draw when it is ready. The Juniors page then shows each placed player as a first name and surname initial.</p>
              <ul class="tag-list" data-junior-draw-pills aria-label="Draw"></ul>
              <div data-junior-draw-sheet></div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <script id="beds-closed-2027" type="application/json" set:html={JSON.stringify(closed2027.entries)} />
          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="beds-closed" hidden>
            <h2>Beds Closed</h2>
            <p class="muted small">The entry list is copied from Sport Manager. Each person is tagged with the year, so they can be picked out and linked.</p>
            <p class="muted small" data-beds-status hidden role="status"></p>
            <div data-beds-list hidden>
              <ul class="tag-list" data-beds-years aria-label="Years"></ul>
              <label class="beds-search">
                Search
                <input type="search" data-beds-search placeholder="Name, email or mobile" />
              </label>
              <p class="muted small" data-beds-count></p>
              <div class="overview-box">
                <table class="overview">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Name</th>
                      <th>Years</th>
                      <th>Grade</th>
                      <th>Email</th>
                      <th>Mobile</th>
                      <th>Paid</th>
                      <th>Login</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody data-beds-rows></tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="scores" hidden>
            <h2>Marking</h2>
            <p class="muted small">Matches marked on the website. PAR to 11, or PAR to 15 for the second division, best of five. The serve starts on the right. The same player moves to the other box. Hand out is a change of server, and that serve starts on the right again. A let is played again. A stroke gives the point. Edit a name here, or open Marking to change the points. Delete removes the match. Sport Manager is not updated from here.</p>
            <h3>In play</h3>
            <p class="muted small">Every match on Match commentary is listed here. Clear takes that one off the list. Clear stale matches takes off every match with no score for an hour.</p>
            <p class="muted small" data-live-status role="status"></p>
            <p class="actions">
              <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-live-clear hidden>Clear stale matches</button>
            </p>
            <div class="overview-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Last score</th>
                    <th>Match</th>
                    <th>Score</th>
                    <th>Marker</th>
                    <th></th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-live-rows></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <h3>Saved</h3>
            <p class="muted small" data-scores-status role="status"></p>
            <div class="overview-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>When</th>
                    <th>Match</th>
                    <th>Score</th>
                    <th>Marker</th>
                    <th></th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-score-rows></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <form class="score-edit" data-score-edit hidden>
              <h3>Edit match</h3>
              <label>
                Player A
                <input data-score-a required />
              </label>
              <label>
                Player B
                <input data-score-b required />
              </label>
              <div data-score-tape></div>
              <p class="actions">
                <button class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" type="submit">Save names</button>
                <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" data-score-open href={url('/captains/score/')}>Change the points</a>
                <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-score-remove>Remove</button>
              </p>
            </form>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="site-sl" hidden>
            <h2>SquashLevels</h2>
            <p class="muted small" data-site-sl-note></p>
            <div data-site-sl></div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="members" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Users</h2>
            <p class="muted small">
              League Master players are listed, and so is anyone with an admin or organiser login. A junior entry adds the player as a JC Player and the parent as a JC Parent. The entry email and phone stay on the parent. The coloured letters show where an email or phone came from. Press a coloured address or number to use the Beds Closed one, or the League Master one. Filter by group or place. LM Club Captain, LM Team Captain, LM Player, JC Player and JC Parent are ticked in Roles and stay as they are. Password opens the login details so you can copy them. Nothing is emailed.
            </p>
            <p class="muted small" data-group-note>Filled from League Master. Each LM Player is listed. Junior entries add a JC Player and a JC Parent.</p>
            <div data-differences hidden>
              <h3>Differences</h3>
              <p class="muted small">League Master has a different email, name, or ES number. The value on this website stays until you choose.</p>
              <div class="overview-box">
                <table class="overview">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Player</th>
                      <th>Field</th>
                      <th>This website</th>
                      <th>League Master</th>
                      <th></th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody data-difference-rows></tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="member-tools">
              <label class="directory-search">
                Search
                <input type="search" data-member-search placeholder="Name, place, email, ES or mobile" autocomplete="off" />
              </label>
              <label>
                Group
                <select data-member-group>
                  <option value="">All groups</option>
                </select>
              </label>
              <label>
                Place
                <select data-member-place>
                  <option value="">All places</option>
                </select>
              </label>
            </div>
            <p class="muted small" data-member-count></p>
            <p class="status" data-users-status role="status"></p>
            <dialog class="account-dialog" data-password-dialog>
              <form method="dialog">
                <p class="muted small">These are the details to send</p>
                <h3 data-password-dialog-who></h3>
                <p class="login-line">Login <strong data-password-dialog-login></strong></p>
                <label>
                  Password
                  <input type="text" readonly data-password-dialog-value autocomplete="off" />
                </label>
                <label class="check-line">
                  <input type="checkbox" data-password-must-change checked />
                  Change this password the next time they sign in
                </label>
                <p class="muted small" data-password-dialog-error></p>
                <div class="actions member-actions">
                  <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-generate-password>Generate</button>
                  <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-copy-dialog-password>Copy details</button>
                  <button class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" type="button" data-apply-password>Set password</button>
                  <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="submit">Close</button>
                </div>
              </form>
            </dialog>
            <div class="role-pop" data-role-pop hidden>
              <p class="role-pop__who" data-role-pop-who></p>
              <div class="role-pop__list" data-role-pop-options></div>
            </div>
            <div class="overview-box users-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <colgroup>
                  <col class="col-name" />
                  <col class="col-place" />
                  <col class="col-email" />
                  <col class="col-roles" />
                  <col class="col-active" />
                  <col class="col-password" />
                  <col class="col-delete" />
                  <col class="col-more" />
                </colgroup>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Name</th>
                    <th>Place</th>
                    <th>Email</th>
                    <th>Roles</th>
                    <th>Active</th>
                    <th>Password</th>
                    <th>Delete</th>
                    <th></th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-users data-group-members></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <nav class="pager" data-users-pager hidden aria-label="User pages">
              <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-users-prev>Previous</button>
              <span data-users-range></span>
              <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-users-next>Next</button>
            </nav>
            <form class="card" data-form="create-account" hidden>
              <div class="card__body stack">
                <h3>Create the login</h3>
                <p class="muted small">Only an admin can create a login. Set the first password and tell them yourself. Nothing is emailed.</p>
                <label>Name <input name="display_name" data-create-name required minlength="2" maxlength="80" autocomplete="off" /></label>
                <label>Email <input name="email" type="email" required data-create-email autocomplete="off" /></label>
                <label>
                  First password
                  <span class="pw-field">
                    <input name="password" type="password" required minlength="8" maxlength="72" autocomplete="new-password" />
                    <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-toggle-password>Show</button>
                  </span>
                  <PasswordRules />
                </label>
                <label>
                  Confirm password
                  <span class="pw-field">
                    <input name="confirm_password" type="password" required minlength="8" maxlength="72" autocomplete="new-password" />
                    <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-toggle-password>Show</button>
                  </span>
                </label>
                <div class="actions member-actions">
                  <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-suggest-password>Suggest a password</button>
                  <button class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" type="submit">Create login</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </form>
            <form class="card" data-form="set-password" hidden>
              <div class="card__body stack">
                <h3>Set a new password for <span data-password-who></span></h3>
                <p class="muted small">They can change this later on their profile. Nothing is emailed.</p>
                <input type="hidden" name="user_id" data-password-user />
                <input type="hidden" name="email" data-password-email />
                <label>
                  New password
                  <span class="pw-field">
                    <input name="password" type="password" required minlength="8" maxlength="72" autocomplete="new-password" />
                    <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-toggle-password>Show</button>
                  </span>
                  <PasswordRules />
                </label>
                <label>
                  Confirm password
                  <span class="pw-field">
                    <input name="confirm_password" type="password" required minlength="8" maxlength="72" autocomplete="new-password" />
                    <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-toggle-password>Show</button>
                  </span>
                </label>
                <div class="actions member-actions">
                  <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-suggest-password>Suggest a password</button>
                  <button class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" type="submit">Save password</button>
                  <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" type="button" data-cancel-password>Cancel</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </form>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="permissions-groups" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Groups</h2>
            <p class="muted small">
              Each group gives one role. The number of people opens the list. Choose a person to update the email, ES number, and phone, and to use the account actions.
            </p>
            <div class="overview-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Group</th>
                    <th>Gives</th>
                    <th>Filled from</th>
                    <th>People</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-permission-groups></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div data-group-people hidden>
              <h3 data-group-people-title></h3>
              <div class="overview-box">
                <table class="overview">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Name</th>
                      <th>Place</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody data-group-people-rows></tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="permissions-roles" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Roles</h2>
            <p class="muted small">A role is the permission its group gives. There is no separate list of people on a role.</p>
            <div class="overview-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Role</th>
                    <th>Given by</th>
                    <th>Can do</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-permission-roles></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="links" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Links</h2>
            <p class="muted small">
              Steve Davies is first. Under him are names already linked where the SquashLevels name is not an exact match. Everyone else has no exact SquashLevels name. Type the name exactly as it appears on SquashLevels. A stored record is used when that name is already here. Otherwise the player is fetched from SquashLevels. Remove a link when it is wrong.
            </p>
            <div class="overview-box">
              <table class="overview">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>LM Player</th>
                    <th>SL</th>
                    <th></th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-links></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="database" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Database</h2>
            <p class="muted small">
              Every public table, with its rows, the space it uses (indexes included), and the newest time stored on it. On disk is the whole database. Each graph is new rows per week for the last six months. A quiet week is a flat line. Only an admin can see this.
            </p>
            <p class="muted small" data-database-status hidden role="status"></p>
            <div data-database hidden>
              <dl class="traffic-kpis">
                <div>
                  <dt>Tables</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="db-tables">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Rows</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="db-rows">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>On disk</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="db-size">—</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <div class="db-charts" data-database-charts></div>
              <h3>Tables</h3>
              <div class="overview-box">
                <table class="overview db-table">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th>Table</th>
                      <th>Rows</th>
                      <th>Size</th>
                      <th>Newest</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody data-database-tables></tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="integrations" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Integrations</h2>
            <p class="muted small">
              Each outside service, the account it signs in with, and how much it has stored here. Passwords stay in GitHub. Each ntfy topic is public. League Master, SquashLevels, other job notes, failures, juniors, County Closed scores and match commentary each have their own.
            </p>
            <p class="muted small" data-integrations-status hidden role="status"></p>
            <div class="overview-box" data-integrations hidden>
              <table class="overview db-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Service</th>
                    <th>Account</th>
                    <th>Password</th>
                    <th>Rows</th>
                    <th>Size</th>
                    <th>When</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody data-integrations-rows></tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="admin-panel" data-tab="traffic" data-lm-only hidden>
            <h2>Site traffic</h2>
            <p class="muted small">
              Each page keeps its own hit count. A hit stores the page, the time, the IP address, the browser, the language, where they came from, and the person when that browser is signed in. Visitors today is one line per IP address. A hit with no IP stays on its own line. Only an admin can see this. A signed-in name opens that person on Users.
            </p>
            <p class="muted small" data-traffic-status hidden role="status"></p>
            <div class="traffic-stats" data-traffic-stats hidden>
              <dl class="traffic-kpis">
                <div>
                  <dt>Page views (7 days)</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="views-7">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Sessions (7 days)</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="sessions-7">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Page views (30 days)</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="views-30">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Sessions (30 days)</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="sessions-30">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Sign-ins (7 days)</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="signins-7">—</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Sign-ins (30 days)</dt>
                  <dd data-kpi="signins-30">—</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <h3>Visitors today</h3>
              <div class="overview-box">
                <table class="overview traffic-table">
                  <thead>
                    <tr>
                      <th><span class="sr-only">Pages</span></th>
                      <th>Who</th>
                      <th>Hits</th>
                      <th>IP address</th>
                      <th>Browser</th>
                      <th>Came from</th>
                      <th>Latest</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
